When formatting the date, you can use the null-conditional operator (`?.`) to call `ToShortDateString()` only when `Birth` has a value:

```csharp
var dob = Birth?.ToShortDateString();
```

Just make sure that `Birth` is declared as a nullable `DateTime` (`DateTime?`) in your model as well.

Also, depending on what you want to do with `dob`, you could consider using the null-coalescing operator (`??`) to provide a fallback value, or use an explicit `HasValue` check:

```csharp
var dob = Birth?.ToShortDateString() ?? "";
```

```csharp
var dob = Birth.HasValue
    ? Birth.Value.ToShortDateString()
    : "";
```


